
1. Introduction

Software testing is an essential part of software development that ensures applications work correctly and reliably. In large software projects, developers need a systematic way to measure how much of the code is tested. Test coverage analysis helps identify untested parts of the application and improves software quality.

This project, titled “Test Coverage Dashboard”, was developed to visually analyze Python code coverage using automated testing tools and graphical dashboards. The system integrates multiple Python libraries such as pytest, coverage.py, matplotlib, and Flask to generate detailed coverage reports and display them in an interactive dashboard.

The dashboard provides developers with:

File-wise coverage percentage
Missing or uncovered lines
Visual coverage graphs
Highlighted low-coverage modules

The project helps improve software reliability, maintainability, and debugging efficiency.

2. Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

To automate Python unit testing using Pytest.
To measure code coverage using Coverage.py.
To parse coverage data into a structured format.
To visualize coverage statistics using graphs.
To highlight uncovered files and missing lines.
To display all analytics through a Flask-based web dashboard.
