4. System Architecture

The project follows a simple modular architecture:

Python Source Files
Sample Python modules are created for testing.
Unit Testing Layer
Pytest executes test cases for the source files.
Coverage Analysis Layer
Coverage.py calculates code coverage and generates JSON reports.
Data Processing Layer
Coverage data is parsed using Python and Pandas.
Visualization Layer
Matplotlib creates graphical charts.
Dashboard Layer
Flask displays coverage reports and graphs through a browser interface.
5. Project Implementation
Step 1: Creating Sample Python Modules

Two sample modules were created:

calculator.py
string_utils.py

These files contain functions such as addition, subtraction, palindrome checking, and string reversal.

Step 2: Writing Unit Tests

Separate test files were written using Pytest:

test_calculator.py
test_string_utils.py

Each function was tested using assertions to verify correctness.

Example:

def test_add():
    assert add(2, 3) == 5
Step 3: Running Coverage Analysis

Coverage analysis was executed using the following commands:

coverage run -m pytest
coverage json -o coverage_data.json

This generated:

.coverage
coverage_data.json

The JSON file contains:

Covered lines
Missing lines
File-wise coverage percentage
Step 4: Parsing Coverage Data

Python scripts were used to extract coverage statistics from the JSON report.

The parsed data included:

File name
Coverage percentage
Missing lines

The data was converted into a Pandas DataFrame for easier analysis.

Step 5: Visualizing Coverage Reports

Matplotlib was used to generate bar charts showing:

Coverage percentage by file
Low-coverage modules

The chart was saved as:

static/coverage_chart.png
Step 6: Building the Dashboard

A Flask web application was developed to display:

Coverage charts
Coverage tables
Missing lines
Uncovered files

The dashboard highlights files with incomplete coverage for easier debugging and testing improvements.

